# Inversion Test Point (XOR ITP) — Fault Coverage Study in BIST Environment

A simulation study evaluating the effectiveness of **XOR Inversion Test Points (ITP)** in improving stuck-at fault coverage for **Built-In Self-Test (BIST)** environments using ITC'99 benchmark circuits and Synopsys TetraMAX ATPG.

---

## Overview

This project investigates how strategically inserted XOR-based inversion test points improve random pattern fault coverage in scan-inserted circuits. Two node selection methodologies are implemented and compared:

- **Method 1 — Raw SCOAP:** Nodes ranked directly by CC0 or CC1 value
- **Method 2 — Weighted Scoring:** Nodes ranked by a weighted combination of controllability asymmetry, absolute hardness, and observability

The study is conducted on three ITC'99 benchmark circuits: **b14**, **b15**, and **b17**, with fault coverage measured before and after ITP insertion at multiple test point counts (5, 10, 15).

---

